      ],
      "observed": "Every VDD power pin of both MCUs is placed in an automatically generated unconnected net. Neither the +3.3V nor the +3V3 net contains FCC1 or NAVC1 VDD pins; for example FCC1 pin 11 is only in unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11), and NAVC1 pin 19 is only in unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19).",
      "expected": "The specification states that the 3V3 rail feeds both MCUs: \"3V3 feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs\". MCU VDD/power_in pins should be connected to the 3.3V supply net, not left unconnected.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"217\") (name \"unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"277\") (name \"unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3V3 feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The FCC and NAVC microcontrollers are unpowered as represented by the netlist, so the flight-control and navigation functions cannot operate.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["REG2"],
      "pins": ["REG2.1"],
      "nets": ["+3.3V", "+3V3"],
      "observed": "The LDO output is on the +3.3V net (REG2 pin 1, OUT), but many 3.3V pull-up resistors, connector pins, switches, SWD pins, U11 VCC, and NAVC1 VBAT are on a separate +3V3 net. No node in the netlist connects +3.3V to +3V3.",
      "expected": "The design specification describes one 3.3V rail produced by LD39200PU33R for the MCUs and sensors. +3V3 and +3.3V should be the same physical supply net or explicitly joined by a component; otherwise the +3V3 domain is floating.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3.3V\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"REG2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"OUT\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"+3V3\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "An LD39200PU33R LDO, fed from the 5 V rail, produces 3V3 for \"MCUs and Sensors\""
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The +3V3 side of the supply network is not powered by the LDO, leaving pull-ups, programming/debug interfaces, boot switches, and some MCU-related supply pins floating or unpowered.",
      "confidence": 0.92
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["U11", "FCC1", "U1", "U2", "U3"],
      "pins": ["U11.4", "FCC1.46", "U1.6", "U2.27", "U3.3"],
      "nets": ["I2C2_SDA_FCC", "Net-(U11-Pad2)", "unconnected-(FCC1-PB10-Pad46)"],
      "observed": "The I2C2_SDA_FCC net is driven by U11 pin 4, the output of a 74LVC1G34 described as a \"Single Buffer Gate\". The same net contains the SDA pins of INA219, PCA9685, and the FCC EEPROM, but it does not contain an MCU pin. FCC1 pin 46 (PB10) is explicitly no-connect, and the MCU is only connected to U11's input on Net-(U11-Pad2).",
      "expected": "An I2C SDA line must be bidirectional/open-drain and directly connected to the MCU's I2C SDA pin so the MCU can drive low, release the bus, and read ACKs. A unidirectional buffer output cannot correctly implement an I2C SDA line.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(libpart (lib \"74xGxx\") (part \"74LVC1G34\") (description \"Single Buffer Gate, Low-Voltage CMOS\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"41\") (name \"I2C2_SDA_FCC\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"4\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"179\") (name \"unconnected-(FCC1-PB10-Pad46)\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "FCC-side I2C2 communication with the current/power sensor, PWM driver, and EEPROM would fail or be corrupted because the MCU cannot properly read or acknowledge on the SDA line.",
      "confidence": 0.78
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows major deviations from the intended design: both MCU VDD pins are unconnected, the 3V3 rail is split into unconnected +3.3V and +3V3 nets, and the FCC I2C SDA line is driven by a unidirectional buffer instead of the MCU. These conditions would make the board nonfunctional or severely limit its communication and programming interfaces."
}

